  "releaseNotes": "## Summary\n\nValtuutus 2.3.0 bounds how long the cache can serve an answer that misses a write committed out of order, makes the cache durations configurable, and moves every clock read in the data layer to .\n\n## Changes that need attention\n\n- **Caching default changed:** a result read at a snap token younger than the new settle window (5 s by default) is now cached for 1 s instead of 5 minutes. Repeated requests at the newest token re-run the engine about once per second for the first few seconds after a write, then cache for the full duration again. Set  to keep the previous behaviour.\n- ** signature:** it now takes an optional . Calls compile unchanged; libraries compiled against 2.2.x that call  need a recompile.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Settle window (#349):** writers take their transaction id before they commit, so concurrent writes can commit out of order and land rows at a token older than one already read. A result cached at that newer token used to miss them for up to 5 minutes; it now expires within a second.\n  - Token age comes from the ULID timestamp in the snap token; tokens that are not ULIDs count as settled.\n  - Writes slower than the window (long transactions you own) can still be missed: keep them short, raise the window, or pass the snap token  returns.\n- **Configurable cache durations (#351):**  (cached results) and  (the latest token, which bounds how long requests without a token can miss a write made outside Valtuutus). Both default to 5 minutes.\n\n\n\n- ** (#350, #352):** the caching settle window, the tombstone reaper (retention watermark and pause between batches), and every writer (transaction ids and ) read the clock from the  registered in the service collection, or  when none is.  gains a constructor that takes a ; existing constructors are unchanged.\n\nSee  for the settle window, its cost in cache hits, clock skew, and the durations.\n\n## Pull requests\n\n- #349 fix(caching): cache results at young snap tokens briefly\n- #350 refactor(data): read the reaper's clock from TimeProvider\n- #351 feat(caching): configurable result and latest-token durations\n- #352 refactor(data): read the writers' clock from TimeProvider",
